# core.autocrlf is on in this repo. Without this, git would check the vendored Cesium tree
# out with CRLF line endings, so a fresh clone would NOT be byte-identical to the npm
# package: `npm run vendor` would report every text file as modified and every sha256 in
# cesium-manifest.txt would be wrong. Store and check out the vendored bytes verbatim.
/public/vendor/** -text
/cesium-manifest.txt -text
